T13 is done and committed.

## What I built

The diff is now a property of the turn, not an instruction to the model.

- `src/facet/generation-0/workspace-diff.ts` (new): after the model stops, the harness runs `git --no-pager diff HEAD` through the turn's own `ExecutionEnv` — the same project capability the tools used — and returns bounded content or the reason git could not answer.
- `facet-turn.ts` runs it whenever the turn published a `tool-start` for `bash`, `edit`, or `write`, then publishes a `diff` (or `diff-unavailable`) frame **before** the single terminal frame.
- The prompt sentence that asked the model to run `git diff` is deleted; the prompt now tells the model not to spend a tool call on one.
- The Supervisor proves and forwards both new frame kinds on the same terms as a tool result.

## What the tests prove now

No test supplies the diff text it asserts. `GitDiffExecBackend` answers only the harness's exact command, by diffing the real file bytes the turn wrote through the capability. Checks include: an `edit` turn with no `bash` call at all still gets a real `-`/`+` diff; a command that changes nothing yields an empty diff; a command that rewrites 4,000 real lines yields a bounded frame marked truncated; a non-zero exit yields `diff-unavailable` with git's own message. The cross-isolate test in `project-turn.test.ts` sees its own write come back as a diff.

